 r←Test_Server_424(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;html;id
⍝ Ask for the list of packages with a version number in the package ID; pretends to be a Browser.
⍝ The page lists packages rather than versions, so there is nothing it could show: 404. It used
⍝ to answer with an INDEX ERROR, because the list it got held one release rather than one package
⍝ per row.
⍝ A package name and no package ID at all must still be listed.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 :For id :In 'example-Goo-2' 'example-Goo-2.1' 'example-Goo-2.1.0'
     html←404 ∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages/',id
     →T.PassesIf∨/'carries a version number'⍷html
 :EndFor

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages/example-Goo'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'example-Goo'⍷html
 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'example-Goo'⍷html

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
